# kills: print controls are never on a card face, and the panel is not inside header/main/footer/card
# suite: node --test --test-name-pattern print.controls.are.never.on.a.card.face..and.the.panel.is.not.inside.header.main.footer.card tests/e2e.test.js
# Context refreshed 2026-09-29 (M2, "add scale into the settings panel"):
# #decks no longer carries the "+ ADD" chip (it moved into the panel's Scales
# group, see #panel-scales-group below). Neither that nor anything else about
# the panel's own content changes what this mutant demonstrates: moving the
# scrim + panel markup back inside <header>, before its closing tag, instead
# of leaving it as a header sibling. Every control the panel carries still
# works exactly the same way (openPanel/closePanel don't care where the
# nodes live in the DOM), so nothing about clicking the trigger, tabbing
# through the panel or downloading a PDF regresses - but the panel would go
# inert whenever something else marks <header> inert, and it would be
# exposed to any header-scoped CSS or landscape layout rule that was never
# written with a modal dialog in mind. Only the ancestry assertion sees it.
